<title>FRANCE: Paris Jan-May import air cargo rises 3.7 pct - ADP.</title>
<headline>Paris Jan-May import air cargo rises 3.7 pct - ADP.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Paris CDG and Orly airports handled 221,613 tonnes of import air cargo traffic between January-May 1997, an increase of 3.7 percent on the same period last year, Aeroports de Paris (ADP) figures show.</p>
<p>The Paris airports' January-May 1997 import traffic, in tonnes, by region, with percentage change on January-May 1996, was as follows:</p>
<p>  Domestic		11,046 tonnes    down 12.5 percent</p>
<p>  European Union	27,887	     up   14.1</p>
<p>  Non-EU Europe	  5,107	     up   12.7</p>
<p>  North Africa	   4,556	     down 19.6</p>
<p>  Sub-Saharan Africa  23,721	     up    0.4</p>
<p>  North America	 70,585	     down  6.8</p>
<p>  French territories   6,365	     up   10.9</p>
<p>  Latin America	  9,214	     up   12.1</p>
<p>  Middle East	   10,531	     up    1.2</p>
<p>  Far East		52,601	     up   23.4</p>
<p>  Total		  221,613	     up    3.7</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017</p>
<p>www.racs.com</p>
</text>
